<title>USA: FOCUS - Sun move reflects struggle for profit.</title>
<headline>FOCUS - Sun move reflects struggle for profit.</headline>
<byline>Laney Salisbury</byline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sun Co Inc's decision on Friday to keep idle one of its Marcus Hook, Penn. refinery units for an extra month is a smart move in a tough market but also reflects the company's ongoing struggle to turn a profit, analysts said Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;The market conditions up to the last three or four days have been awful,&quot; said industry analyst Mark Gilman of UBS Securities. &quot;To optimize downtime in a period like this makes a lot of sense.&quot;</p>
</text>
